It is useful to separate each charge from the spatial shape of its field, $\mathbf E_i=q_i\widehat{\mathbf E}_i,$ although nothing depends on keeping the hat notation. With both charges present, linearity gives $\mathbf{E}=\mathbf{E}_1+\mathbf{E}_2.$ Apart from the choice of units, the electrostatic field energy has the form $U_{\text{field}}\propto\int d^3x\,\mathbf{E}^2.$ Substituting the sum of the two fields gives $\begin{aligned}
U_{\text{field}}
&\propto\int d^3x\,(\mathbf{E}_1+\mathbf{E}_2)^2 \\
&\propto\int d^3x\,\bigl(\mathbf{E}_1^2+\mathbf{E}_2^2
  +2\mathbf{E}_1\!\cdot\!\mathbf{E}_2\bigr).\end{aligned}$

