The same-flavor states are neutral, but neither receives a separate particle name by itself. Quantum mechanics permits us to superpose them. The two normalized, orthogonal combinations are $\begin{aligned}
\ket{\pi^0} &\approx \frac{\ket{\bar u u}-\ket{\bar d d}}{\sqrt2},\\
\ket{\eta} &\approx \frac{\ket{\bar u u}+\ket{\bar d d}}{\sqrt2}.\end{aligned}$

